    "body": "This whole section seems bad currently (https://output-wtmypyildq.now.sh/dev/workers.html#apis-available-to-workers), and I don't think this is a good fix since it refers to interfaces which do not exist in the dev edition. (Names of mixins are not developer-facing.) Rather I think maybe:\r\n\r\n- We need to add a domintro for `importScripts(urls)`, `navigator`, and `location`\r\n- We need to add some w-nohtml section references, maybe, for WorkerNavigator?\r\n- Non-worker-navigator needs some sections exposed to the dev edition; I don't see concurrent hardware or onLine in https://output-wtmypyildq.now.sh/dev/system-state.html#system-state-and-capabilities\r\n- WorkerLocation needs to include some kind of section reference instead of the current very-UA-facing text. Your additions below are a good start.\r\n\r\nI can work on that soon.",
